diff --git a/NOSH_PATCH.md b/NOSH_PATCH.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..b9dccfb6ee8129e0fca26fe9b60f7527d0d3a809
--- /dev/null
+++ b/NOSH_PATCH.md
@@ -0,0 +1,113 @@
+# nosh Reedline adaptation
+
+Base: upstream Reedline **0.52.0**, MIT licensed, Git commit
+`61d430801c86455bdec5946bbfb09fec211275e3`.
+The corresponding published archive SHA256 is
+`3798f88894590a7acdc9a25936605efbde199641f31e8d99248fce72e535638a`.
+The package requires Rust 1.95; nosh builds with the repository-pinned Rust 1.98.1.
+
+This replaces the 0.51 fixed-footer adaptation. There is no reserved footer,
+scrolling-region lease, second input reader, or alternate-screen frontend.
+
+## Renderer repair
+
+`painting/display.rs`, `painting/painter.rs`, `painting/mod.rs` and the mouse
+snapshot wiring in `engine.rs` import the isolated, verified 0.52 repair.
+It tracks painted physical rows and temporarily archived owned prefixes during
+resize, clips long input by physical rows and graphemes, maps mouse positions
+through that viewport, and retains complete submitted/cancelled transcripts.
+Literal tabs are retained through ANSI stripping and expanded in painting copies
+to eight-column stops, including wrapped tab cells and continuation-prompt
+offsets. Layout, viewport clipping, painted-row reflow and mouse-to-source byte
+mapping share that walk. Editable and submitted buffer bytes remain unchanged;
+the terminal is sent spaces for painted tabs, not raw HT with host-dependent
+margin behavior.
+The imported repair's portable patch SHA256 is
+`5dc972065b9b2a3486613eb439d6af9cfb0c022c5b8c4f6fb5bb4bb6aa6e08c5`.
+
+That repair passed the recorded WSL, Windows and tmux visible-screen/input
+cases. It does **not** guarantee zero draft fragments in tmux native history.
+The historical fixture is not proof that the nosh integration passes.
+
+## Host integration
+
+- `Prompt::update_context` receives borrowed buffer and interaction facts
+  (including the current selection) before painting and hint generation.
+  Its default is a no-op. The host composes ordinary prompt
+  text; this interface neither paints nor reserves any terminal rows.
+- `with_menu_submit_protection(true)` keeps nosh's 0.51 submit boundary:
+  Enter in an active empty/provisional menu closes it without executing the
+  buffer. The upstream default and explicit `MenuAccept` remain unchanged.
+- `with_contextual_input(true)` dispatches each raw event against the current
+  input owner, including within rapid batches. The default remains disabled.
+  EditMode wrappers can forward contextual parsing, mode control and the
+  post-event observation without maintaining another buffer or focus machine.
+- Contextual reverse search accepts with validation on Enter, has distinct
+  accept-for-edit/cancel events, and restores the originating buffer/cursor/
+  selection/mode on cancel. Prompt context exposes the actual completion point
+  separately from a Vi caret.
+- `CompleteOrHostCommand` returns a host action only for a final empty menu;
+  provisional results never fall through. The host diagnoses completer errors
+  and decides whether its fallback capability is available.
+- Host draft replacement is one undo point with the initiating mode retained.
+  Suspended contextual batches retain remaining text but do not submit it before
+  the user can review the host result.
+- Vi has opt-in pending-sequence/effective-repeat limits, checked before event
+  expansion (including cached dot actions), and masks for rebound native
+  u/p/P/? aliases. Cancellation remains available with an unfinished operator.
+  Ordinary AltGr text preserves its original case. Keyboard protocol setup/
+  cleanup failures are returned or diagnosed, not silently accepted.
+
+## Asynchronous completion contract
+
+- `CompletionResult::Limited` carries selectable, current partial/truncated
+  suggestions and a bounded single-line menu reason. It is provisional for
+  uniqueness, common-prefix insertion and host fallback, not stale input.
+  `Unavailable` terminates a failed/disabled query without declaring no matches.
+- `Completer` has default-compatible request, navigation/edit, cancellation and
+  automatic-insertion authorization hooks. All menu arrows/pages revoke host
+  authorization. Editing, history/search, mode changes, host actions, direct
+  menu closure, read-line termination/errors and editor drop end or revoke the
+  corresponding interaction; late results cannot reopen a cancelled menu.
+  A suspended host guard notice retains menu/search focus while cancelling its
+  background work; an actual host draft replacement also closes the menu.
+- Deferred insertion pins the buffer, cursor, edit revision, selection, mode
+  and menu. Only an unchanged explicit request may accept a final unique value
+  or extend a common prefix. A refresh never grants insertion authorization.
+- `Suggestion::completion_id` identifies the logical selected object across
+  refreshes. `ColumnarMenu` retains that object through reordering, description
+  changes, column changes and resize. A disappeared selection stays visibly
+  invalid until explicit navigation, rather than accepting a different item.
+  Batched navigation applies every movement before the single repaint.
+- `Menu::accept_selected` and `AcceptedCompletion` report only a guarded current
+  selection, including the actual inserted range. Legacy menus remain compatible.
+  `Completer::completion_accepted` defaults to `CompletionAcceptance::Continue`;
+  an already-expanded choice can return `SuppressAbbreviationExpansion`.
